+// spelling and stops before inspecting the ceiling directory, matching Git's
+// discovery boundary. It deliberately does not resolve alternate spellings in
+// that case: resolving caller-provided ceiling entries could touch an off-volume
+// path, while resolving only dir could bypass a ceiling spelled through a link.
+// If no ceiling can be proven to contain the lexical spelling, the fallback
+// declines discovery rather than risk crossing such an alias.
+func discoverImplicitCheckoutRoot(dir string) (string, bool) {
+	var ceilings []string
