// and adds the new one.
//
// Ignored files are excluded (git omits them without --ignored), matching the
// provider's working-tree walk, which honours .gitignore. The tracked-file
// comparison is raw and deliberately bypasses Git's conversion machinery: no
// repository-configured clean or process filter can execute. That can report a
// converted, CRLF, sparse, or mode-configured checkout dirty even when porcelain
// status would call it clean; false-dirty is the safe result for this cache gate.
func WorktreeDirtyPaths(ctx context.Context, repo string) ([]string, error) {
